    "name": "Folk forward roll (3+3+2)",
    "genres": ["organicVibes", "ballad"],
    "rationale": "A folk fingerpicking roll that groups the eighth notes three, three and two, so the thumb's bass notes land on beat 1, the 'and' of 2 and beat 4 instead of on every beat. It gives an acoustic song a rolling, slightly lopsided drive that sits well under a singer-songwriter vocal and is clearly different from steady alternating-bass picking. Three takes: the plain roll, the same roll with the top string pinched together with each bass note, and a 16th-note roll in groups of three for choruses that ends with a soft brush into the next bar.",
